From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: comctl32: a selected icon is drawn as custom draw says

An application that clears CDIS_SELECTED in its item pre-paint gets the item
drawn unselected, icon included: the icon was blended with the highlight
colour (ILD_SELECTED) from the item's own state whatever custom draw said.
File Explorer tints only the row, so its icons turned purple. Large icons and
tiles are drawn over whatever is behind them, so a box custom draw tinted
stays tinted around a picture.

Gate: test/explorer2-gate.sh (a selected picture keeps its pixels).
---
--- a/dlls/comctl32/listview.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/listview.c
@@ -5416,13 +5416,18 @@
 
         TRACE("iImage=%d\n", item->iImage);
 
-        if (item->state & (LVIS_SELECTED | LVIS_CUT) && infoPtr->bFocus)
+        /* Stained Glass: what custom draw left of the selected state decides,
+         * so an application that clears CDIS_SELECTED gets an unblended icon */
+        if (((nmlvcd->nmcd.uItemState & CDIS_SELECTED) || (item->state & LVIS_CUT)) && infoPtr->bFocus)
             style = ILD_SELECTED;
         else
             style = ILD_NORMAL;
 
+        /* Stained Glass: a large icon or a tile's picture is drawn over whatever is behind it
+         * (custom draw may have tinted the whole box), not over the list's background */
         ImageList_DrawEx(himl, item->iImage, nmlvcd->nmcd.hdc, rcIcon.left, rcIcon.top,
-                         rcIcon.right - rcIcon.left, rcIcon.bottom - rcIcon.top, infoPtr->clrBk,
+                         rcIcon.right - rcIcon.left, rcIcon.bottom - rcIcon.top,
+                         infoPtr->uView == LV_VIEW_ICON || infoPtr->uView == LV_VIEW_TILE ? CLR_NONE : infoPtr->clrBk,
                          item->state & LVIS_CUT ? RGB(255, 255, 255) : CLR_DEFAULT,
                          style | (item->state & LVIS_OVERLAYMASK));
     }
